            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-57433",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-57433"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-57433?s=debian&n=perl&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "Storable versions before 3.41 for Perl have a signed integer overflow when deserializing a crafted SX_HOOK record.  retrieve_hook_common reads a signed 32-bit item count from an SX_HOOK record and calls av_extend with that count plus one. A count of I32_MAX wraps the addition to a negative value.  A crafted blob passed to thaw or retrieve triggers the overflow; av_extend receives the negative count and dies with a panic, terminating the deserialization.\n\n---\n- perl 5.40.1-8 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1138906; bug #1142035)\n[trixie] - perl 5.40.1-6+deb13u1\n- libstorable-perl <removed>\nhttps://lists.security.metacpan.org/cve-announce/msg/41780100/\nFixed by: https://github.com/Perl/perl5/commit/e4f681784bcdeaa91ff02a2fa4cdcae5c46779d7 (v5.43.11)\n",
                "markdown": "> Storable versions before 3.41 for Perl have a signed integer overflow when deserializing a crafted SX_HOOK record.  retrieve_hook_common reads a signed 32-bit item count from an SX_HOOK record and calls av_extend with that count plus one. A count of I32_MAX wraps the addition to a negative value.  A crafted blob passed to thaw or retrieve triggers the overflow; av_extend receives the negative count and dies with a panic, terminating the deserialization.\n\n---\n- perl 5.40.1-8 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1138906; bug #1142035)\n[trixie] - perl 5.40.1-6+deb13u1\n- libstorable-perl <removed>\nhttps://lists.security.metacpan.org/cve-announce/msg/41780100/\nFixed by: https://github.com/Perl/perl5/commit/e4f681784bcdeaa91ff02a2fa4cdcae5c46779d7 (v5.43.11)\n\n|                                                                                                        |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/perl@5.36.0-7%2Bdeb12u3?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                      |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                               |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "UNSPECIFIED",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl@5.36.0-7%2Bdeb12u3?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "UNSPECIFIED"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-7017",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-7017"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-7017?s=debian&n=perl&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "HTTP::Tiny versions before 0.095 for Perl forward credential headers to cross-origin redirect targets.  When the server returns a 3xx redirect, `_maybe_redirect` follows the `Location:` header and `_prepare_headers_and_cb` re-merges the caller's `headers` argument into the new request, without checking whether the redirect target shares an origin with the original URL. Caller-supplied `Authorization`, `Cookie` and `Proxy-Authorization` headers are therefore re-sent to whatever host the redirect names, across scheme, host or port boundaries, and including `https` to `http` downgrades that expose them in plaintext on the wire.  The HTTP::Tiny POD note that \"Authorization headers will not be included in a redirected request\" applied only to the URL-userinfo Basic-auth path, not to headers passed explicitly by the caller.\n\n---\n- libhttp-tiny-perl 0.096-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1141638)\n[trixie] - libhttp-tiny-perl 0.090-1+deb13u1\n[bookworm] - libhttp-tiny-perl <postponed> (Minor issue; leak requires caller-supplied credential headers and an attacker-influenced redirect)\n[experimental] - perl 5.44.0-1\n- perl 5.42.3-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1141639)\n[trixie] - perl 5.40.1-6+deb13u1\nhttps://lists.security.metacpan.org/cve-announce/msg/41618211/\nhttps://github.com/Perl-Toolchain-Gang/HTTP-Tiny/pull/36\nFixed by: https://github.com/Perl-Toolchain-Gang/HTTP-Tiny/commit/84984ef3930ddd4afcf5eb83b40d3cee200739c3 (release-0.095)\nFixed by: https://github.com/Perl-Toolchain-Gang/HTTP-Tiny/commit/e7a03aedf2395158f2b0d3bad2df943349227bb3 (release-0.095)\nFixed by: https://github.com/Perl-Toolchain-Gang/HTTP-Tiny/commit/8f32ca89e21c3ad0422adc698fa6ad17a193f55f (release-0.095)\n",
                "markdown": "> HTTP::Tiny versions before 0.095 for Perl forward credential headers to cross-origin redirect targets.  When the server returns a 3xx redirect, `_maybe_redirect` follows the `Location:` header and `_prepare_headers_and_cb` re-merges the caller's `headers` argument into the new request, without checking whether the redirect target shares an origin with the original URL. Caller-supplied `Authorization`, `Cookie` and `Proxy-Authorization` headers are therefore re-sent to whatever host the redirect names, across scheme, host or port boundaries, and including `https` to `http` downgrades that expose them in plaintext on the wire.  The HTTP::Tiny POD note that \"Authorization headers will not be included in a redirected request\" applied only to the URL-userinfo Basic-auth path, not to headers passed explicitly by the caller.\n\n---\n- libhttp-tiny-perl 0.096-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1141638)\n[trixie] - libhttp-tiny-perl 0.090-1+deb13u1\n[bookworm] - libhttp-tiny-perl <postponed> (Minor issue; leak requires caller-supplied credential headers and an attacker-influenced redirect)\n[experimental] - perl 5.44.0-1\n- perl 5.42.3-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1141639)\n[trixie] - perl 5.40.1-6+deb13u1\nhttps://lists.security.metacpan.org/cve-announce/msg/41618211/\nhttps://github.com/Perl-Toolchain-Gang/HTTP-Tiny/pull/36\nFixed by: https://github.com/Perl-Toolchain-Gang/HTTP-Tiny/commit/84984ef3930ddd4afcf5eb83b40d3cee200739c3 (release-0.095)\nFixed by: https://github.com/Perl-Toolchain-Gang/HTTP-Tiny/commit/e7a03aedf2395158f2b0d3bad2df943349227bb3 (release-0.095)\nFixed by: https://github.com/Perl-Toolchain-Gang/HTTP-Tiny/commit/8f32ca89e21c3ad0422adc698fa6ad17a193f55f (release-0.095)\n\n|                                                                                                        |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/perl@5.36.0-7%2Bdeb12u3?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                      |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                               |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "UNSPECIFIED",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl@5.36.0-7%2Bdeb12u3?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "UNSPECIFIED"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2005-2541",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2005-2541"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2005-2541?s=debian&n=tar&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "Tar 1.15.1 does not properly warn the user when extracting setuid or setgid files, which may allow local users or remote attackers to gain privileges.\n\n---\nThis is intended behaviour, after all tar is an archiving tool and you\nneed to give -p as a command line flag\n- tar <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=328228; unimportant)\n",
                "markdown": "> Tar 1.15.1 does not properly warn the user when extracting setuid or setgid files, which may allow local users or remote attackers to gain privileges.\n\n---\nThis is intended behaviour, after all tar is an archiving tool and you\nneed to give -p as a command line flag\n- tar <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=328228; unimportant)\n\n|                                                                                                              |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/tar@1.34%2Bdfsg-1.2%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                            |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                     |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/tar@1.34%2Bdfsg-1.2%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2007-5686",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2007-5686"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2007-5686?s=debian&n=shadow&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "initscripts in rPath Linux 1 sets insecure permissions for the /var/log/btmp file, which allows local users to obtain sensitive information regarding authentication attempts.  NOTE: because sshd detects the insecure permissions and does not log certain events, this also prevents sshd from logging failed authentication attempts by remote attackers.\n\n---\n- shadow <unfixed> (unimportant)\nSee #290803, on Debian LOG_UNKFAIL_ENAB in login.defs is set to no so\nunknown usernames are not recorded on login failures\n",
                "markdown": "> initscripts in rPath Linux 1 sets insecure permissions for the /var/log/btmp file, which allows local users to obtain sensitive information regarding authentication attempts.  NOTE: because sshd detects the insecure permissions and does not log certain events, this also prevents sshd from logging failed authentication attempts by remote attackers.\n\n---\n- shadow <unfixed> (unimportant)\nSee #290803, on Debian LOG_UNKFAIL_ENAB in login.defs is set to no so\nunknown usernames are not recorded on login failures\n\n|                                                                                                                    |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/shadow@1%3A4.13%2Bdfsg1-1%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                                  |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                           |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/shadow@1%3A4.13%2Bdfsg1-1%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2010-0928",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2010-0928"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2010-0928?s=debian&n=openssl&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E%3D3.0.11-1%7Edeb12u2",
              "help": {
                "text": "OpenSSL 0.9.8i on the Gaisler Research LEON3 SoC on the Xilinx Virtex-II Pro FPGA uses a Fixed Width Exponentiation (FWE) algorithm for certain signature calculations, and does not verify the signature before providing it to a caller, which makes it easier for physically proximate attackers to determine the private key via a modified supply voltage for the microprocessor, related to a \"fault-based attack.\"\n\n---\nhttp://www.eecs.umich.edu/~valeria/research/publications/DATE10RSA.pdf\nhttps://github.com/openssl/openssl/discussions/24540\nFault injection based attacks are not within OpenSSLs threat model according\nto the security policy: https://www.openssl.org/policies/general/security-policy.html\n",
                "markdown": "> OpenSSL 0.9.8i on the Gaisler Research LEON3 SoC on the Xilinx Virtex-II Pro FPGA uses a Fixed Width Exponentiation (FWE) algorithm for certain signature calculations, and does not verify the signature before providing it to a caller, which makes it easier for physically proximate attackers to determine the private key via a modified supply voltage for the microprocessor, related to a \"fault-based attack.\"\n\n---\nhttp://www.eecs.umich.edu/~valeria/research/publications/DATE10RSA.pdf\nhttps://github.com/openssl/openssl/discussions/24540\nFault injection based attacks are not within OpenSSLs threat model according\nto the security policy: https://www.openssl.org/policies/general/security-policy.html\n\n|                                                                                                         |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/openssl@3.0.20-1~deb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12  |\n|Affected range  >=3.0.11-1~deb12u2                                                                       |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">=3.0.11-1~deb12u2",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
