            {
              "id": "CVE-2015-9019",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2015-9019"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2015-9019?s=debian&n=libxslt&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "In libxslt 1.1.29 and earlier, the EXSLT math.random function was not initialized with a random seed during startup, which could cause usage of this function to produce predictable outputs.\n\n---\n- libxslt <unfixed> (unimportant; bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=859796)\nhttps://bugzilla.gnome.org/show_bug.cgi?id=758400\nhttps://bugzilla.suse.com/show_bug.cgi?id=934119\nThere's no indication that math.random() in intended to ensure cryptographic\nrandomness requirements. Proper seeding needs to happen in the application\nusing libxslt.\n",
                "markdown": "> In libxslt 1.1.29 and earlier, the EXSLT math.random function was not initialized with a random seed during startup, which could cause usage of this function to produce predictable outputs.\n\n---\n- libxslt <unfixed> (unimportant; bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=859796)\nhttps://bugzilla.gnome.org/show_bug.cgi?id=758400\nhttps://bugzilla.suse.com/show_bug.cgi?id=934119\nThere's no indication that math.random() in intended to ensure cryptographic\nrandomness requirements. Proper seeding needs to happen in the application\nusing libxslt.\n\n|                                                                                                           |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/libxslt@1.1.35-1%2Bdeb12u4?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                         |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                  |\n"
              },
