              "help": {
                "text": "Kerberos 5 (aka krb5) 1.21.2 contains a memory leak vulnerability in /krb5/src/lib/gssapi/krb5/k5sealv3.c.\n\n---\n- krb5 <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1098754; unimportant)\nhttps://github.com/LuMingYinDetect/krb5_defects/blob/main/krb5_detect_2.md\nFixed by: https://github.com/krb5/krb5/commit/c5f9c816107f70139de11b38aa02db2f1774ee0d\nCodepath cannot be triggered via API calls, negligible security impact\nhttps://mailman.mit.edu/pipermail/kerberos/2024-March/023095.html\n",
                "markdown": "> Kerberos 5 (aka krb5) 1.21.2 contains a memory leak vulnerability in /krb5/src/lib/gssapi/krb5/k5sealv3.c.\n\n---\n- krb5 <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1098754; unimportant)\nhttps://github.com/LuMingYinDetect/krb5_defects/blob/main/krb5_detect_2.md\nFixed by: https://github.com/krb5/krb5/commit/c5f9c816107f70139de11b38aa02db2f1774ee0d\nCodepath cannot be triggered via API calls, negligible security impact\nhttps://mailman.mit.edu/pipermail/kerberos/2024-March/023095.html\n\n|                                                                                                        |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/krb5@1.20.1-2%2Bdeb12u5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                      |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                               |\n"
