            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-86141",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-86141"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-86141?s=debian&n=libxml2&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "xmlregexp in libxml2 before 2.15.4 has a NULL pointer dereference in xmlRegNewParserCtxt after a strdup failure, i.e., it does not calculate a string length after NULL checking.\n\n---\n- libxml2 2.15.4+dfsg-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1146744)\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/work_items/1107\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/e89a8aae4c9b40cdafcf66b3f9e57c62db37bb55 (v2.15.4)\n",
                "markdown": "> xmlregexp in libxml2 before 2.15.4 has a NULL pointer dereference in xmlRegNewParserCtxt after a strdup failure, i.e., it does not calculate a string length after NULL checking.\n\n---\n- libxml2 2.15.4+dfsg-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1146744)\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/work_items/1107\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/e89a8aae4c9b40cdafcf66b3f9e57c62db37bb55 (v2.15.4)\n\n|                                                                                                                  |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/libxml2@2.9.14%2Bdfsg-1.3~deb12u6?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                                |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                         |\n"
