                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-102473",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-102473"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-102473?s=debian&n=dash&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in dash. When built without libc fnmatch, the internal pmatch() matcher implements * by unbounded recursion over candidate positions. A local user who can plant filenames, or otherwise feed that matcher, can make a short multi-star pattern such as *.*.*.*.*.tar.gz consume excessive CPU.\n\n---\n- dash <unfixed>\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2543005\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in dash. When built without libc fnmatch, the internal pmatch() matcher implements * by unbounded recursion over candidate positions. A local user who can plant filenames, or otherwise feed that matcher, can make a short multi-star pattern such as *.*.*.*.*.tar.gz consume excessive CPU.\n\n---\n- dash <unfixed>\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2543005\n\n|                                                                                              |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/dash@0.5.12-2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                            |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                     |\n"
