            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-76781",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-76781"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-76781?s=debian&n=libxml2&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in libxml2. A local user or an attacker providing a specially crafted XML catalog can trigger a NULL pointer dereference during XML catalog parsing. This occurs when a `nextCatalog` element lacks its mandatory `catalog` attribute, leading to the application crashing and causing a Denial of Service (DoS).\n\n---\n- libxml2 2.15.4+dfsg-1\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/merge_requests/442\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/c63248941708bc1d2e3a4292954593312212f6ca (master)\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/a34c084d7a576914c1424caabdaaf5e227bb39ef (v2.15.4)\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in libxml2. A local user or an attacker providing a specially crafted XML catalog can trigger a NULL pointer dereference during XML catalog parsing. This occurs when a `nextCatalog` element lacks its mandatory `catalog` attribute, leading to the application crashing and causing a Denial of Service (DoS).\n\n---\n- libxml2 2.15.4+dfsg-1\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/merge_requests/442\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/c63248941708bc1d2e3a4292954593312212f6ca (master)\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/a34c084d7a576914c1424caabdaaf5e227bb39ef (v2.15.4)\n\n|                                                                                                                  |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/libxml2@2.9.14%2Bdfsg-1.3~deb12u6?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                                |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                         |\n"
              },
