              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-39823"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-39823?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.25.10",
              "help": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-27142 fixed a vulnerability in which URLs were not correctly escaped inside of a <meta> tag's <content> attribute. If the URL content were to insert ASCII whitespaces around the '=' rune inside of the <content> attribute, the escaper would fail to similarly escape it, leading to XSS.\n",
                "markdown": "> CVE-2026-27142 fixed a vulnerability in which URLs were not correctly escaped inside of a <meta> tag's <content> attribute. If the URL content were to insert ASCII whitespaces around the '=' rune inside of the <content> attribute, the escaper would fail to similarly escape it, leading to XSS.\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.24.6  |\n|Affected range  <1.25.10                  |\n|Fixed version   1.25.10                   |\n"
              },
