                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-78409",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-78409"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-78409?s=debian&n=util-linux&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "The X-mount.subdir option uses a detached-tree fast path on Linux 6.15 and later and passes the configured subdirectory to open_tree() with AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW. That flag does not stop intermediate symlink traversal or keep resolution inside the newly mounted filesystem. A local unprivileged user with an fstab-authorized X-mount.subdir entry can attach a host path at the intended mountpoint.\n\n---\n- util-linux 2.42.3-1\n[trixie] - util-linux <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/security/advisories/GHSA-8f2p-47x3-43mv\n",
                "markdown": "> The X-mount.subdir option uses a detached-tree fast path on Linux 6.15 and later and passes the configured subdirectory to open_tree() with AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW. That flag does not stop intermediate symlink traversal or keep resolution inside the newly mounted filesystem. A local unprivileged user with an fstab-authorized X-mount.subdir entry can attach a host path at the intended mountpoint.\n\n---\n- util-linux 2.42.3-1\n[trixie] - util-linux <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/security/advisories/GHSA-8f2p-47x3-43mv\n\n|                                                                                                              |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/util-linux@2.38.1-5%2Bdeb12u3?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                            |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                     |\n"
              },
