            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39822",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-39822"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-39822?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.25.12",
              "help": {
                "text": "On Unix systems, opening a file in an os.Root improperly follows symlinks to locations outside of the Root when the final path component of the a path is a symbolic link and the path ends in /.\n\nFor example, 'root.Open(\"symlink/\")' will open \"symlink\" even when \"symlink\" is a symbolic link pointing outside of the root.\n",
                "markdown": "> On Unix systems, opening a file in an os.Root improperly follows symlinks to locations outside of the Root when the final path component of the a path is a symbolic link and the path ends in /.\n\nFor example, 'root.Open(\"symlink/\")' will open \"symlink\" even when \"symlink\" is a symbolic link pointing outside of the root.\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.24.6  |\n|Affected range  <1.25.12                  |\n|Fixed version   1.25.12                   |\n"
