                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-78408",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-78408"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-78408?s=debian&n=util-linux&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "The nsenter --join-cgroup option opens the target cgroup.procs file as root and leaves that file descriptor open across later namespace and credential changes and across execve(). Because the kernel checks later cgroup migrations using the credentials from the original open, a program run in an attacker-controlled target can inherit root's ability to move host processes between cgroups. After a privileged operator uses --join-cgroup against that target, an unprivileged user can migrate and terminate unrelated root processes.\n\n---\n- util-linux 2.42.4-1\n[trixie] - util-linux <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/security/advisories/GHSA-55fx-f4gg-cfhj\nFixed by: https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/commit/286dd3ff41526b582ef48830de239dffbaa61f90 (v2.42.4)\n",
                "markdown": "> The nsenter --join-cgroup option opens the target cgroup.procs file as root and leaves that file descriptor open across later namespace and credential changes and across execve(). Because the kernel checks later cgroup migrations using the credentials from the original open, a program run in an attacker-controlled target can inherit root's ability to move host processes between cgroups. After a privileged operator uses --join-cgroup against that target, an unprivileged user can migrate and terminate unrelated root processes.\n\n---\n- util-linux 2.42.4-1\n[trixie] - util-linux <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/security/advisories/GHSA-55fx-f4gg-cfhj\nFixed by: https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/commit/286dd3ff41526b582ef48830de239dffbaa61f90 (v2.42.4)\n\n|                                                                                                              |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/util-linux@2.38.1-5%2Bdeb12u3?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                            |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                     |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "HIGH",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/util-linux@2.38.1-5%2Bdeb12u3?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.9",
                "tags": [
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-86140",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-86140"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-86140?s=debian&n=libxml2&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "In libxml2 before 2.15.4, xmlSnprintfElements in valid.c has a strcat stack-based buffer overflow.\n\n---\n- libxml2 2.15.4+dfsg-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1146744)\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/d1686f91dbda141a752200419d35639fd6b38340 (v2.15.4)\n",
                "markdown": "> In libxml2 before 2.15.4, xmlSnprintfElements in valid.c has a strcat stack-based buffer overflow.\n\n---\n- libxml2 2.15.4+dfsg-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1146744)\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/d1686f91dbda141a752200419d35639fd6b38340 (v2.15.4)\n\n|                                                                                                                  |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/libxml2@2.9.14%2Bdfsg-1.3~deb12u6?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                                |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                         |\n"
              },
